    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` derived field on `Owner`, following the existing pattern of `@Transient` computed getters (like `getRegion()`, `getLocality()`, `getAgeBand()`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a fixed region-to-timezone table and a `getTimezone()` transient getter that derives the IANA timezone from the owner's locality (region):\n   ```java\n   private static final Map<String, String> REGION_TIMEZONE = Map.of(\n       \"NSW\", \"Australia/Sydney\", \"VIC\", \"Australia/Melbourne\", \"QLD\", \"Australia/Brisbane\");\n\n   @Transient\n   public String getTimezone() {\n       return REGION_TIMEZONE.get(getLocality());\n   }\n   ```\n   Returns `null` (field absent) when the locality isn't one of the three regions.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the Owner schema (next to `locality`). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a matching `timezone` field, which MapStruct auto-maps from `Owner.getTimezone()` \u2014 no mapper change needed since the property names match.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` (Sydney owner, postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`) passes, and the full suite is green.",
